)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Messages -- C to I                       !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
@COMMAND PARM IS MISSING
}    TSO with no command after it.
@DATA SET DISPLAYED
}    ST typed on the output: the Status panel is read again from the top.
@END OF TOPIC
}    Help: Enter on the last panel of a topic. T shows the contents.
@FIELD NOT NUMERIC
}    A priority typed over PRTY holds something other than digits.
@FINDLIM REACHED
}    One FIND looked through FINDLIM lines and stopped. The next FIND goes
}    on from there.
@HELP NOT AVAILABLE
}    The help panels could not be shown: they are not in the ISPPLIB
}    concatenation. The installation guide says where they go.
@INCONSISTENT PARAMETERS
}    FIND with two directions or kinds, or a string longer than its columns.
@INVALID CLASS
}    A class typed over C, SCLASS or CLASSES is not A to Z or 0 to 9.
@INVALID COMMAND
}    SDSF does not know the command, or this panel does not take the action
}    character. It stays where it was typed, to be corrected.
}  Enter: next page   PF7: contents   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHMS3
  &ZUP = ISFHTOC
)END
